    context: "The Hebrew word for covenant is berith, often used with the verb 'cut', because covenants were sealed by a sacrifice. In Genesis 15 God made a covenant with Abram by passing between the pieces of animals, a custom that meant the one who broke the promise would suffer the fate of the animals. The writer of Hebrews uses this event to encourage Christians who were wavering, reminding them that God swore by himself.",
